 Pamidimarri", "text": "", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-22T03:46:02Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "4.\tIn the industrial cities and mill towns of Britain and Ireland, from roughly 1820 well into the 1970s, you could pay a person — sometimes an old woman, sometimes a retired police constable — between sixpence and a shilling per week to perform a service essential to urban factory life. They walked a fixed route in the pre-dawn darkness carrying a long bamboo or hazel pole — sometimes with stiff wires on the end like a fishing rod, sometimes a simple knob — and tapped firmly on the bedroom windows of their clients until they were sure the occupants were awake. Some, like the famous Mary Smith of Limehouse in East London, used a long pea-shooter to fire dried peas at upper-storey windows. Astonishingly, the profession survived more than a century after the invention of the wind-up mechanical alarm clock — partly because workers genuinely did not trust the clock, and partly because someone still had to wake the person who would otherwise wake everyone else. For 10 points, what was this profession called? ‎<attached: 00123296-PHOTO-2026-04-21-20-46-02.jpg>", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-22T03:46:16Z", "username": "Akshay", "text": "Knockers", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-22T03:46:18Z", "username": "Harshvardhan Ranade", "text": "Alarm clock", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-22T03:46:19Z", "username": "Akshay", "text": "Knockers up", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-22T03:46:22Z", "username": "Abhishek Vats", "text": "Knocker upper", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-22T03:46:34Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "Answer: knocker-up or knocker-upper", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-22T03:46:53Z", "username": "Harshvardhan Ranade", "text": "Oh didn't read what the actual last line question was", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-22T03:47:32Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "These were human alarm clocks who went around the neighborhood waking up people", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}]